  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig 5, 'DIIG process for planning and implementing a digital health enterprise'. Seven numbered, colour-coded phases — from 01 assessing the current state and enabling environment to 07 implementing, maintaining and scaling — each with its steps. To the right, resource tiles are placed against the phases they serve and marked as PDF or online, including the WHO–ITU eHealth strategy toolkit, the Digital implementation investment guide, the ITU SDG digital investment framework, TOGAF, OpenHIE, the WHO SMART guidelines with digital adaptation kits, and the WHO MAPS toolkit. 'WHO handbook for health supply chain architecture (this document)' is highlighted twice: spanning phases 02 to 04, and in phase 07. Adapted from the 2020 WHO Digital Implementation Investment Guide.",
